# Stage 12 — Jenkins with AWS

## Objective
Understand how Jenkins can publish artifacts or container images to AWS and automate deployments.

## Suggested learning sequence
1. Understand IAM roles and least-privilege policies.
2. Create a test Amazon ECR repository.
3. Configure an approved AWS identity mechanism for the Jenkins agent.
4. Authenticate to ECR.
5. Build and push a test image.
6. Add deployment to a test environment.
7. Verify the deployed version and document rollback.

Prefer an IAM role or another approved short-lived identity mechanism over long-lived access keys. Never commit credentials. Start with a sandbox and monitor AWS costs.

## Assignment
Draw your proposed pipeline and list the minimum AWS permissions each step requires.
